{
  "name": "measured_corr",
  "scale": 1.0,
  "_comment": [
    "The measured level with the sensing error correlated in time (rho 0.9,",
    "about ten frames), which is what a real pose estimator produces: its error is",
    "dominated by viewpoint, occlusion and calibration, none of which resample every",
    "frame. Same magnitude as measured, so the difference between the two is the",
    "correlation alone -- and filtering, which both the expert and its clone do,",
    "cannot average a correlated error away."
  ],
  "params": {
    "object_half_size": {
      "low": 0.85,
      "high": 1.1,
      "mode": "scale"
    },
    "object_mass": {
      "low": 0.5,
      "high": 2.0,
      "mode": "scale"
    },
    "object_friction": {
      "low": 0.46,
      "high": 1.9,
      "mode": "scale"
    },
    "table_friction": {
      "low": 0.46,
      "high": 1.9,
      "mode": "scale"
    },
    "gripper_gain": {
      "low": 0.7,
      "high": 1.4,
      "mode": "scale"
    },
    "hand_compliance": {
      "low": 0.7,
      "high": 1.8,
      "mode": "scale"
    },
    "action_latency": {
      "low": 1.0,
      "high": 6.0,
      "mode": "absolute"
    },
    "gravity": {
      "low": 0.999,
      "high": 1.001,
      "mode": "scale"
    },
    "obs_noise_pos": {
